        "original_id": "55aa62d6-a7c1-5183-a463-bb9c3a56520d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Baltimore's Marching Ravens, Baltimore Ravens\n- Places: M&T Bank Stadium, Owings Mills, Baltimore, Indianapolis\n- Products: The Band That Wouldn't Die\n- Topics: American football, NFL franchise relocation\n\nFacts:\n- Since 1947, Baltimore's Marching Ravens has supported three separate American football franchises.\n- In 1984, the NFL's Baltimore Colts franchise relocated controversially from Baltimore to Indianapolis.\n- The Band That Wouldn't Die follows the story of Baltimore's Marching Ravens and includes the 1984 Baltimore Colts relocation.\n- Baltimore's Marching Ravens is the official marching band of the Baltimore Ravens American football team.\n- The Baltimore Ravens play their home games at M&T Bank Stadium.\n- The Baltimore Ravens are headquartered in Owings Mills.",
